# Build output. Everything cargo writes is derived from the sources, is large,
# and is different on every machine, so none of it belongs in a repository.
/target

# The launcher's own configuration is personal: it holds the absolute paths to
# your programs and the keys you reserved. The launcher writes an example file
# by itself when it starts without one, so nothing is lost by keeping it out —
# and `git add -f launcher.toml` puts it in anyway if you want to ship yours.
launcher.toml

# Bookkeeping of the editor or agent host that works in this folder. It names
# this checkout locally and means nothing to anybody else.
.freebuff/

# Editors and the operating system leave these behind.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# `rustfmt` and `rustc` backups.
*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock is deliberately *not* ignored: this is an application, not a
# library, so the exact versions that were tested are part of the project.
